{title: 500 - Take Time to Be Holy}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #500 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 500}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Take time to be [Bb]ho[F]ly, Speak [C7]oft with thy [F]Lord;
[F]Abide in Him [Bb]al[F]ways, [C]And [G7]feed on His [C]word;
[C7]Make friends of God's [F]children, [C7]Help those who are [F]weak,
[F]Forgetting in [Bb]nothing [F]His [C7]blessing to [F]seek.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Take [Bb]time [F]to [C7]be [F]holy,
[F][Bb]the [F]world [C][G7]rushes [C]on;
[C7]spend [F]much [C7]time [F]in secret
[F][Bb]with [F][C7]Jesus [F]alone.
[F][Bb]By [F]looking [C7]to [F]Jesus,
[F][Bb]like [F]him [C]thou [G7]shalt [C]be;
[C7]thy [F]friends [C7]in [F]thy conduct
[F][Bb]his [F]likeness [C7]shall [F]see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]Take [Bb]time [F]to [C7]be [F]holy,
[F][Bb]let [F]him [C]be [G7]thy [C]guide,
[C7]and [F]run [C7]not [F]before him,
[F][Bb][F]whatever [C7][F]betide.
[F]In [Bb]joy [F]or [C7]in [F]sorrow,
[F][Bb]still [F]follow [C][G7]the [C]Lord,
[C7]and, [F]looking [C7]to [F]Jesus,
[F]still [Bb]trust [F]in [C7]his [F]word.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]Take [Bb]time [F]to [C7]be [F]holy,
[F][Bb]be [F]calm [C]in [G7]thy [C]soul,
[C7]each [F]thought [C7]and [F]each motive
[F][Bb]beneath [F][C7]his [F]control.
[F]Thus [Bb]led [F]by [C7]his [F]spirit
[F][Bb]to [F]fountains [C][G7]of [C]love,
[C7]thou [F]soon [C7]shalt [F]be fitted
[F][Bb]for [F][C7]service [F]above.
{end_of_verse}
